1
00:01:41,629 --> 00:01:42,880
Engrave it…

2
00:01:49,136 --> 00:01:51,180
Engrave it upon your body.

3
00:01:58,479 --> 00:02:00,606
Engrave it upon the land.

4
00:02:06,570 --> 00:02:08,823
Engrave it upon the sea.

5
00:02:13,869 --> 00:02:16,163
Engrave it upon your enemy.

6
00:02:16,789 --> 00:02:18,666
Engrave it upon your loot.

7
00:02:21,418 --> 00:02:22,753
Engrave it…

8
00:02:23,754 --> 00:02:25,673
Engrave it…

9
00:02:42,106 --> 00:02:45,150
Engrave your warmth upon me.

10
00:03:08,507 --> 00:03:09,550
Einar!

11
00:03:14,221 --> 00:03:15,347
What was that for!

12
00:03:15,431 --> 00:03:17,349
Right back at you.

13
00:03:18,225 --> 00:03:20,853
If you cut that tree
it'll crush our house.

14
00:03:22,605 --> 00:03:26,358
-Are you going to become a woodcutter?
-No, I'm not.

15
00:03:26,442 --> 00:03:30,112
I'm training for battle!
Take a look at my power!

16
00:03:31,280 --> 00:03:32,990
You may be well-built,

17
00:03:33,073 --> 00:03:36,577
but that doesn't mean you can fight.
Now get the food ready!

18
00:03:36,660 --> 00:03:38,996
I'm starving!

19
00:03:43,167 --> 00:03:45,211
More like, don't throw a knife at me.

20
00:03:45,294 --> 00:03:47,796
Pick something else like plates or spoons.

21
00:03:47,880 --> 00:03:49,506
It's okay if it's a plate?

22
00:03:54,762 --> 00:03:57,723
So that's why bears do it.

23
00:03:57,806 --> 00:03:59,808
-Eat a lot before winter.
-Is that so.

24
00:04:05,105 --> 00:04:07,066
-Thanks.
-So, why did you?

25
00:04:07,149 --> 00:04:08,901
Start training all of a sudden?

26
00:04:10,444 --> 00:04:13,697
What else is there,
other than to protect this place.

27
00:04:17,117 --> 00:04:18,911
Everything was reduced to ashes.

28
00:04:19,495 --> 00:04:21,664
But we finally got back on our feet.

29
00:04:23,540 --> 00:04:26,043
Nobody wants to go through that again.

30
00:04:28,337 --> 00:04:29,797
Even Dad--

31
00:04:31,590 --> 00:04:34,051
Guttorm's milk is delicious!

32
00:04:34,134 --> 00:04:36,971
I know, right? That man knows

33
00:04:37,054 --> 00:04:39,306
how to handle teats.

34
00:04:39,390 --> 00:04:41,433
What's with those fingers? How creepy!

35
00:04:41,517 --> 00:04:42,518
I'm talking here!

36
00:04:43,102 --> 00:04:45,062
-Ew!
-Don't think about it.

37
00:04:45,145 --> 00:04:46,772
Don't involve yourself with warriors.

38
00:04:49,441 --> 00:04:52,736
Aren't you frustrated with
being on the losing end all the time?

39
00:04:52,820 --> 00:04:55,990
Dad died to protect us, you know.

40
00:04:56,073 --> 00:04:58,993
That's right. And that's why you're alive.

41
00:04:59,076 --> 00:05:00,619
You rebuilt the village

42
00:05:00,703 --> 00:05:03,205
and are eating a delicious meal
with two beauties.

43
00:05:08,002 --> 00:05:09,420
We haven't lost.

44
00:05:58,510 --> 00:06:01,388
Listen, once you enter the forest,
just run for your life.

45
00:06:01,472 --> 00:06:02,306
Follow the river…

46
00:06:03,599 --> 00:06:04,808
Róta…

47
00:06:05,809 --> 00:06:06,643
Mom…

48
00:06:17,029 --> 00:06:19,823
Don't think about anything.
Just run straight ahead.

49
00:06:20,824 --> 00:06:22,743
Your brother and mother are with you.

50
00:06:58,862 --> 00:07:00,072
Mom!

51
00:07:09,164 --> 00:07:10,916
Ready? I'll lift you up.

52
00:07:14,211 --> 00:07:15,712
Mom!

53
00:07:24,513 --> 00:07:26,849
Einar, run away.

54
00:07:27,724 --> 00:07:31,019
-Leave me behind.
-Don't be stupid!

55
00:07:32,438 --> 00:07:34,982
Forget that! Just try to stand up!

56
00:07:35,065 --> 00:07:35,983
Mom?

57
00:07:36,900 --> 00:07:38,235
Mom!

58
00:07:45,951 --> 00:07:47,286
Mom!

59
00:07:50,497 --> 00:07:51,790
Stupid girl…

60
00:07:54,418 --> 00:07:57,463
Hey, there are still people over there.

61
00:07:58,088 --> 00:08:01,467
Oh, I see a woman too. Here we come!

62
00:08:14,313 --> 00:08:15,856
Stand up, Einar.

63
00:08:17,649 --> 00:08:19,902
Take Róta… Hurry!

64
00:08:21,695 --> 00:08:22,738
Mom…

65
00:08:25,908 --> 00:08:27,659
I may be a dying old lady…

66
00:08:28,535 --> 00:08:29,703
but I can do this much.

67
00:08:31,955 --> 00:08:33,207
Make it out alive…

68
00:08:36,418 --> 00:08:38,420
As long as you're alive…

69
00:08:39,046 --> 00:08:40,339
you can start again…

70
00:08:50,140 --> 00:08:52,476
Einar…

71
00:08:53,894 --> 00:08:55,062
Róta…

72
00:09:15,791 --> 00:09:17,876
Why aren't they running away?

73
00:09:17,960 --> 00:09:20,379
Hey, she's pretty cute.

74
00:09:21,463 --> 00:09:23,715
Your mama died, right?

75
00:09:25,467 --> 00:09:27,386
-Róta!
-Let go!

76
00:09:27,469 --> 00:09:29,012
-Einar!
-Róta!

77
00:09:29,638 --> 00:09:31,181
Let go of her!

78
00:09:32,766 --> 00:09:34,142
Einar!

79
00:09:35,269 --> 00:09:36,895
I won't forgive you! How dare you!

80
00:09:38,397 --> 00:09:41,358
-Einar!
-How sad.

81
00:09:50,951 --> 00:09:52,327
How dare you--

82
00:10:02,713 --> 00:10:05,549
Hey! What are you doing?!

83
00:10:06,133 --> 00:10:08,260
She stabbed me with something!

84
00:10:09,344 --> 00:10:10,512
What a waste.

85
00:10:10,596 --> 00:10:14,558
Oh well. Let's sell this kid
and get some drinks with that money.

86
00:10:15,309 --> 00:10:17,853
-You're such an idiot!
-I'm sorry, okay?

87
00:10:18,478 --> 00:10:21,189
Come on, drink money.

88
00:11:19,373 --> 00:11:21,583
A FIR TREE STANDING ON BARREN LAND DIES
WITH NO BARK NOR LEAVES TO SHELTER IT

89
00:11:21,666 --> 00:11:23,710
SO IS A MAN WHOM NO ONE LOVES

90
00:11:23,794 --> 00:11:26,338
WHY SHOULD HE KEEP ON LIVING?
EXCERPT FROM HÁVAMÁL

91
00:12:08,422 --> 00:12:09,339
How is she?

92
00:12:12,717 --> 00:12:14,344
This is no good.

93
00:12:15,178 --> 00:12:16,346
Damn it.

94
00:12:16,430 --> 00:12:18,473
We have no choice. Help me carry her.

95
00:12:30,902 --> 00:12:32,654
Ready…

96
00:12:34,865 --> 00:12:36,324
Hey!

97
00:12:46,877 --> 00:12:49,171
Hey! What are you doing?!

98
00:12:49,254 --> 00:12:50,839
You didn't have to throw her out!

99
00:12:55,969 --> 00:12:58,096
Good, it's not inflamed.

100
00:13:00,640 --> 00:13:04,561
We'll pass out fur blankets.
Keep your bodies warm.

101
00:13:05,228 --> 00:13:07,689
We spent a fortune on you all.

102
00:13:07,772 --> 00:13:10,567
Don't you dare become sick
without our approval.

103
00:13:11,526 --> 00:13:15,071
At least stay healthy
until we find a buyer for you. Got that?

104
00:13:18,700 --> 00:13:21,620
Hurry up! We have to furl the sail!

105
00:13:49,564 --> 00:13:50,482
That's right…

106
00:13:51,775 --> 00:13:53,068
I have to live…

107
00:14:03,912 --> 00:14:07,749
Make sure to drink alcohol.
It'll give you a healthy complexion.

108
00:14:08,458 --> 00:14:11,503
Wash every nook and cranny.
Especially your hair.

109
00:14:12,295 --> 00:14:14,381
Get rid of each other's lice.

110
00:14:18,885 --> 00:14:21,596
How is that?

111
00:14:22,389 --> 00:14:26,852
Her hair is fine.
Do her makeup so she looks younger.

112
00:14:41,408 --> 00:14:44,786
How about it? We have
a pretty good lineup, don't we?

113
00:14:45,453 --> 00:14:47,205
They're all so-so.

114
00:14:47,289 --> 00:14:51,209
Don't say that.
We have the best of the best.

115
00:14:54,337 --> 00:14:57,465
That's right… I can't just stay there!

116
00:14:58,174 --> 00:15:01,803
If I can get out of here alive,
I can start again…

117
00:15:24,618 --> 00:15:26,244
Up we go…

118
00:15:28,997 --> 00:15:30,540
A thief!

119
00:15:31,416 --> 00:15:32,792
Sorry!

120
00:15:39,507 --> 00:15:40,675
Hey, Einar.

121
00:15:41,760 --> 00:15:44,679
It seems like you still don't get it.

122
00:15:52,103 --> 00:15:56,149
All right, you slaves. Listen carefully.

123
00:15:56,858 --> 00:15:59,694
Your homelands are far, far away.

124
00:15:59,778 --> 00:16:02,197
You can't return even if you try.

125
00:16:02,280 --> 00:16:06,910
And of course,
no one will help you run away.

126
00:16:07,535 --> 00:16:11,831
That's because you're foreign, penniless,

127
00:16:12,415 --> 00:16:14,084
slaves!

128
00:16:14,167 --> 00:16:17,837
Get someone nice to buy you
and do your best to serve them.

129
00:16:18,672 --> 00:16:22,592
You'll get to eat nice meals, which you
won't if you escape and become a beggar.

130
00:16:22,676 --> 00:16:26,846
Before you venture out,
think about which life is more favorable.

131
00:16:28,139 --> 00:16:30,392
Got that, Einar?

132
00:16:45,490 --> 00:16:46,574
I…

133
00:16:48,118 --> 00:16:49,202
will…

134
00:16:50,829 --> 00:16:51,997
…live!

135
00:16:59,087 --> 00:17:00,672
Yeah…

136
00:17:01,339 --> 00:17:03,174
He's not bad,

137
00:17:03,258 --> 00:17:05,885
but don't you have one with a cuter face?

138
00:17:05,969 --> 00:17:08,471
I see! If that's the case,

139
00:17:08,555 --> 00:17:11,266
I have a special one just for you.

140
00:17:11,349 --> 00:17:14,269
Is that so? How exciting.

141
00:17:14,352 --> 00:17:17,230
I'm sure you will love it.

142
00:17:22,861 --> 00:17:24,529
They are right.

143
00:17:25,613 --> 00:17:26,948
Even if I recklessly escape

144
00:17:27,699 --> 00:17:29,284
I won't have anyone to help me.

145
00:17:30,994 --> 00:17:32,037
Besides…

146
00:17:35,498 --> 00:17:36,374
I don't…

147
00:17:37,584 --> 00:17:40,462
have anywhere to go anymore.

148
00:17:42,589 --> 00:17:43,590
If I just…

149
00:17:45,050 --> 00:17:47,469
give in and become an obedient pet…

150
00:17:49,721 --> 00:17:53,266
My goodness, you sure are lucky.

151
00:17:53,349 --> 00:17:55,518
We just restocked a bunch of them.

152
00:17:55,602 --> 00:17:57,020
Look, that's him.

153
00:17:59,230 --> 00:18:01,399
He's what you're looking for, right?

154
00:18:27,926 --> 00:18:30,553
He's completely different!

155
00:18:30,637 --> 00:18:32,847
He's neither blond nor small!

156
00:18:32,931 --> 00:18:35,975
How weird…
Now that I take a good look, he's not.

157
00:18:36,559 --> 00:18:39,062
Well, anyhow, what do you think about him?

158
00:18:39,145 --> 00:18:41,481
He's strong and sturdy. If you buy now--

159
00:18:41,564 --> 00:18:45,860
Like I said, I'm not here to buy a worker!

160
00:18:46,486 --> 00:18:49,072
I just want to free a relative of mine.

161
00:18:49,155 --> 00:18:52,742
I'm pretty sure he ended up in this town.

162
00:18:52,826 --> 00:18:56,371
He's blond and small
and his name is Thorfinn.

163
00:18:56,454 --> 00:18:59,249
Are you sure you have no clue where he is?

164
00:19:07,048 --> 00:19:08,299
Sorry about that.

165
00:19:11,261 --> 00:19:12,512
Sorry to waste your time.

166
00:19:12,595 --> 00:19:15,515
No worries. Please come again.

167
00:19:17,976 --> 00:19:19,769
He'll never find him.

168
00:19:22,856 --> 00:19:27,110
So he's asking around
in search of his relative, huh?

169
00:19:30,989 --> 00:19:33,491
Whoever has someone like that
searching for him

170
00:19:34,033 --> 00:19:35,410
is so fortunate.

171
00:19:40,290 --> 00:19:41,624
You there.

172
00:19:46,379 --> 00:19:49,716
Can you understand me? Show me your teeth.

173
00:20:03,271 --> 00:20:06,816
-What's your name?
-It's Einar.

174
00:20:06,900 --> 00:20:09,110
Where are you from
and what was your profession?

175
00:20:09,694 --> 00:20:12,071
I was a farmer in the north of England.

176
00:20:22,415 --> 00:20:26,336
Einar, what do you think about
helping out with my field?

177
00:20:34,594 --> 00:20:35,929
Field?

178
00:20:59,202 --> 00:21:01,454
Einar, this way!

179
00:21:05,833 --> 00:21:08,002
All of my servants are working now.

180
00:21:08,086 --> 00:21:11,923
-I'll introduce you during dinnertime.
-Yes, sir.

181
00:21:13,549 --> 00:21:16,010
First, take a look at my farm.

182
00:21:47,750 --> 00:21:52,171
Hey, Mom, are you sure?

183
00:21:54,674 --> 00:21:57,677
I don't even have the freedom to choose

184
00:21:57,760 --> 00:21:59,804
life or death anymore.

185
00:22:01,431 --> 00:22:02,890
Can you still say

186
00:22:04,392 --> 00:22:06,311
that we haven't lost?

187
00:22:30,501 --> 00:22:31,961
My family was killed

188
00:22:32,628 --> 00:22:36,090
and I lost everything
including my homeland.

189
00:22:37,800 --> 00:22:39,343
I didn't even know

190
00:22:40,178 --> 00:22:42,013
what I was living for.

191
00:22:50,938 --> 00:22:54,233
Thorfinn! It's me! Can you come out?

192
00:23:10,625 --> 00:23:12,543
I must be bought by a kind master

193
00:23:13,711 --> 00:23:15,922
and do my very best to serve him.

194
00:23:17,590 --> 00:23:21,385
As long as I stay obedient,
I won't go hungry.

195
00:23:22,804 --> 00:23:25,807
I was starting to believe that.

196
00:23:26,307 --> 00:23:28,142
Thorfinn?

197
00:23:39,987 --> 00:23:40,905
In any case,

198
00:23:43,324 --> 00:23:48,204
that was when I met Thorfinn
for the first time.

199
00:25:37,730 --> 00:25:39,106
"Ketil's farm."

200
00:25:39,190 --> 00:25:40,942
Subtitle translation by: Kiko Morita
